WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Cooling openings. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Relate apertures to plausible functions

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: An opening’s visual shape does not prove its function. Treat a cooling claim as a hypothesis until the air path is supported.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Mark a possible inlet and outlet, then sketch a continuous route through the heat exchanger before calling it a duct.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Evidence matching

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: A view supports interpretation; it cannot prove hidden structure or compliance alone.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Relate apertures to plausible functions
